7.8 support — retained vector paths
Authorization: 9672c660 (paths), ca2ead18 (measured vector policy).
Reference: lab commit 4141a78; renderer.md §4.4a. No lab reference edits.

Mechanism / files:
bbt-ui-model/src/draw/path.rs — Move/Line/Cubic, stroke width/dash/cap/join,
validation, independent cubic-extrema bounds and endpoints; std only.
draw/prim.rs and list.rs — retained Path command, transform and validation.
bbt-ui/src/components.rs — L6 Path viewport, points, stroke, paint and opacity;
layout and group scaling preserve the record, paint emits Prim::Path.
bbt-render/src/chrome/paths.rs — lyon_tessellation =1.0.22, CPU stroke tessellation
and nonzero union to remove internal overlap edges; cached device-owned edge
buffers, keyed by shape/stroke, reused across paint/translation/scale changes.
paths.wgsl — analytic polygon area in each pixel (clamped edge integral), one
sRGB source-over operation per stroke. Supports regular/zero-length round dashes,
widths, caps and joins; clips, groups and ordered foreground remain in force.
chrome/mod.rs — split Path at its ordered position, preserving enclosing clips;
non-Path galleries keep the existing renderer branch. Terminal cells untouched.
Lyon crates are MIT OR Apache-2.0; float_next_after 1.0.0 MIT. Cargo.lock adds
only those four packages and the bbt-render edge; foreign mux dependencies are
not staged. The lock write was coordinated with Rook (0bd02fae, cc8d0354).

bboxybook/src/paths.rs — public UI.Path constructor records in caller-owned
slots; no SVG path internals or browser child positions feed tessellation.
capture-inputs.js computes web geometry independently from the public commands;
native snapshots read the retained draw commands and use model path_geometry.
capture.mjs identifies current paths, captures their shared enclosing backdrop,
and hashes paths.html. main/lib/parity dispatch the gallery and exact geometry.
README documents bboxybook paths and its policy.

Measurements / acceptance:
Initial SDF ramp: 48/48 over the old 0.1% budget, worst 1.3364%.
Measured SVG viewport-origin snapping reduced the worst to 0.2852%; analytic
area coverage retained thin strokes/corners, worst 0.2857716120%.
The 1.5px Skia stroke and cap/curve AA residue is logged, not tuned away.
Oracle ca2ead18 decided paths: 0.5% pixels + image read + exact public-input
bounds/endpoints; text and other non-text budgets unchanged. Policy unit test
rejects missing geometry and even 0.000001px error. Cubic test proves the true
interior extremum (7.5), not the control-hull bound (10).

